# Dedicated Settings Window Implementation Plan

We will implement a dedicated standalone Electron window for **Settings & Configurations** that opens when clicking the bottom-left settings gear icon (or pressing `Ctrl+,` / via MenuBar). The window will feature a custom cyber-dark titlebar, comprehensive categorized preferences, and live two-way IPC synchronization with the main editor.

---

## Proposed Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Main Window / Activity Bar Settings Icon] -->|IPC: cortex:settings:open| B[Electron Main Process]
    B -->|Create or Focus| C[Settings BrowserWindow<br/>760x540 Frameless]
    C -->|Loads '#/settings'| D[SettingsWindow UI Component]
    D -->|IPC: cortex:settings:update| B
    B -->|Broadcast to Main Window| A
```

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Multi-Window Route Handling**: We will use Hash Routing (`#/settings`) within the Vite renderer bundle. In dev mode it loads `http://localhost:5173/#/settings`, and in production it loads `loadFile('.../index.html', { hash: '/settings' })`. This guarantees zero build-configuration breakages and works seamlessly in both dev and production packaged builds.
> - **Single-Instance Settings Window**: If the user clicks Settings while the settings window is already open, it will smoothly un-minimize and focus the existing window rather than spawning duplicate windows.

